 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A book for «التوراة» (twice, each leaving before the next clause). No motif on the prophets, rabbis or scholars. 44:33-41 keeps the condition both tafsirs give: ruling by other than revelation is kufr that removes one from the religion when one holds it lawful (As-Sa'di adds it may otherwise be a major sin). Al-Muyassar's first-person «اخشوني», «أنزلت» not used. STAGING v4: 43 stays ambient: those who come to the Prophet for judgment and turn from his ruling (behaviour toward him). 44: a town by day; a group (those who were Jews) sits on 44:13 to be judged and taught; the prophets of 44:9 are not drawn (no figure may stand for them, so the teacher enters only on 44:14). One man stands for the rabbis and scholars (Al-Muyassar: those who teach people the law): he speaks to the group on 44:15 and holds the book on 44:19 (what they were entrusted with). Everyone leaves on 44:24, before the commands and the prohibition (44:24-32) and before the ruling on whoever does not judge by revelation (44:33-41), which play on the empty town with the two-paths plate, so nobody on stage is labelled by it."
 },
